  "comments": "An undistinguishable variant exists for year 1993, with slightly different alloy (Aluminium 97% + Magnesium 3%) - 56,000 pieces were made. They were all released to circulation and are supposed to be more shiny than usual.<br /><br />\r\nKM# 3.1 (smaller signature &quot;vo&quot;-mark, obverse: lion&#039;s crown more pointy and a bit farther from the letter &quot;E&quot;)<br />\r\nKM# 3.2 (larger signature &quot;vo&quot;-mark, obverse: lion&#039;s crown flatter and a bit closer to the letter &quot;E&quot;)<br />\r\nSince 2000, obverse lettering changed from Bold to Double lined.<br /><br />\r\nDifferent mintmarks (castle = (HM), Hamburg Mint, crowned &quot;b&quot; = Bizuterie Jablonec Czech Mint)<br /><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/56dc956bc262c.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/56dc956bc262c.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nAlloy is Aluminium with 1% of Magnesium.",
